A vulnerability has been found in <a href="https://vuldb.com/product/aapanel">aaPanel up to 8.25.0</a> and classified as <a href="https://vuldb.com/kb/risk">very critical</a>. The affected element is the function <code>ExecShell</code> of the file <em>class/public/common.py</em> of the component <em>File Manager</em>. The manipulation of the argument <em>sfile/dfile/access/user</em> leads to os command injection.

This vulnerability is uniquely identified as <a href="https://vuldb.com/cve/CVE-2026-113506">CVE-2026-113506</a>. The attack is possible to be carried out remotely. Moreover, an exploit is present.

The vendor confirms: &quot;The reported RCE and LFI vulnerabilities require authentication.&quot;

A vulnerability, which was classified as <a href="https://vuldb.com/kb/risk">problematic</a>, was found in <a href="https://vuldb.com/product/aapanel">aaPanel up to 8.25.0</a>. Impacted is the function <code>send_file</code> of the file <em>BTPanel/routes/v2.py</em> of the component <em>Download Endpoint</em>. Executing a manipulation of the argument <em>filename</em> can lead to path traversal.

This vulnerability is handled as <a href="https://vuldb.com/cve/CVE-2026-113505">CVE-2026-113505</a>. The attack can be executed remotely. Additionally, an exploit exists.

The vendor confirms: &quot;The reported RCE and LFI vulnerabilities require authentication.&quot;

A vulnerability described as <a href="https://vuldb.com/kb/risk">problematic</a> has been identified in <a href="https://vuldb.com/product/tibillet:lespass">TiBillet Lespass up to 10e87909c5d526dffa6d424c104fc12860740537</a>. This vulnerability affects the function <code>get_img_from_url</code> of the file <em>ApiBillet/serializers.py</em> of the component <em>APIv1</em>. Executing a manipulation of the argument <em>img_url/image_url</em> can lead to server-side request forgery.

This vulnerability is tracked as <a href="https://vuldb.com/cve/CVE-2026-112358">CVE-2026-112358</a>. The attack can be launched remotely. No exploit exists.

The vendor confirms: &quot;[T]he fix (destination IP validation, redirect re-checks, timeout and size limit on remote image download) is already planned in our v2 API, which replaces the affected v1 endpoints. The v1 API, including the three affected serializers, will be removed in our next major release.&quot;

A vulnerability described as <a href="https://vuldb.com/kb/risk">problematic</a> has been identified in <a href="https://vuldb.com/product/donetick">donetick up to 0.1.82</a>. The impacted element is the function <code>CanDeleteHistory</code> of the file <em>internal/chore/model/model.go</em> of the component <em>History Deletion Handler</em>. The manipulation of the argument <em>AssignedTo</em> results in improper authorization.

This vulnerability is reported as <a href="https://vuldb.com/cve/CVE-2026-112045">CVE-2026-112045</a>. The attack can be launched remotely. Moreover, an exploit is present.

The project maintainer explains: &quot;The concerns about &quot;IDOR&quot; framing seem to be overstated in my opinion (...), as Circle members are already trusted collaborators. We will address this issue. However, since the impact is limited to trusted members within the same circle, I would classify this as a bug rather than a security vulnerability.&quot;
